---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';

/** Address for privacy requests. Single source for every mailto link on this page. */
const CONTACT_EMAIL = 'hello@worthsheet.com';
const mailto = `mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('WorthSheet privacy request')}`;
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | WorthSheet"
  description="How WorthSheet collects and uses your name, email, ZIP code and analytics data when you download the free PFS template, and the choices you have."
  path="/privacy-policy/"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy policy', path: '/privacy-policy/' }]}
>
  <Section>
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <Eyebrow>Legal</Eyebrow>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="muted policy-date">
        Effective <time datetime="2026-11-06">November 6, 2026</time>
      </p>

      <Prose>
        <p>
          WorthSheet (“we”, “us”) runs worthsheet.com, a website with a free personal financial
          statement template, calculators, guides and a bank finder. This policy explains what
          personal data the site handles, why, who else receives it, and the choices you have. We
          keep it short because we collect very little.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Our website address is https://worthsheet.com. To ask a question about this policy or
          make a privacy request, email <a href={mailto}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Data</th>
                <th scope="col">When</th>
                <th scope="col">Why</th>
                <th scope="col">Where it goes</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Name and email (required)</th>
                <td>You submit the template form on <a href={url('/download/')}>/download/</a>.</td>
                <td>To deliver the template and to contact you about it.</td>
                <td>A Google Sheet we operate, plus an email notification to the WorthSheet team.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">ZIP code and purpose (optional)</th>
                <td>You fill in the optional form fields.</td>
                <td>To understand who uses the template and for what (mortgage, SBA or business loan, personal loan, financial advisor, other).</td>
                <td>The same Google Sheet and notification email.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Page and referrer</th>
                <td>Sent automatically with the form.</td>
                <td>To see which page and source a signup came from.</td>
                <td>The same Google Sheet.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Analytics data (page views, events)</th>
                <td>Only after you click Accept in the cookie banner.</td>
                <td>To understand how the site is used and improve it.</td>
                <td>Google Analytics 4.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Your cookie choice</th>
                <td>When you click Accept or Decline.</td>
                <td>To remember your choice.</td>
                <td>Your browser only (see “Cookies and local storage”).</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">ZIP code for bank search</th>
                <td>You search for banks by ZIP code on <a href={url('/banks/')}>/banks/</a>.</td>
                <td>To look up FDIC-insured institutions near you.</td>
                <td>The FDIC, directly from your browser (see below).</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          We do not ask for financial account numbers, Social Security numbers or the figures you
          put into the template. The calculators on this site run in your browser; the numbers you
          type into them are not sent to us.
        </p>

        <h2>The template form</h2>
        <p>
          When you submit the form, your browser sends the fields above directly to a Google Apps
          Script web app that we operate. The script saves them as a new row in a Google Sheet that
          only the WorthSheet team can open, and sends an email notification with your name, email,
          ZIP code, purpose and page to the WorthSheet team through Google’s mail service. Google
          therefore also receives the technical data any web request includes, such as your IP
          address and browser details, under <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google’s Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>We use this information to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>deliver the template and confirm that your request was saved;</li>
          <li>
            send you occasional template updates, or contact you about the template you requested
            (every message gives you a way to opt out, or you can email us);
          </li>
          <li>understand the main use cases of the template, so we can improve it and our guides.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The form includes a hidden anti-spam field; it is not stored. If JavaScript is turned off
          the form still works but shows you the raw confirmation response instead of the template
          links; you can then return to this site and open the template from the
          <a href={url('/')}>home page</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Opening the template in Google Sheets or Excel</h2>
        <p>
          After you submit the form we send you to Google, which asks you to sign in to make your
          own copy of the Google Sheet. Your copy lives in your Google account and is governed by
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/terms" rel="noopener">Google’s Terms of Service</a>
          and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Privacy Policy</a>, not by
          this policy. We do not see or receive what you type into your copy. The Excel (.xlsx)
          version downloads to your device and stays there.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
        <p>
          WorthSheet does not set cookies of its own. The only item we store in your browser is
          your cookie choice, saved in local storage under the key <code>ws-consent</code> with the
          value <code>granted</code> or <code>denied</code>. It stays until you clear your browser
          data. Use “Cookie settings” in the footer to review or change your choice at any time.
        </p>
        <h3>Google Analytics 4</h3>
        <p>
          We use Google Analytics 4 (measurement ID G-RVHR897PTG) with Google Consent Mode v2.
          Every consent signal starts as denied and Google’s analytics script is not loaded at all
          until you click Accept. If you accept, we grant only <code>analytics_storage</code>, which lets
          Google Analytics set cookies (such as <code>_ga</code>) and measure page views and
          interactions. Advertising storage, advertising user data and ad personalization stay
          denied, and we do not use Google Analytics for advertising. If you click Decline, or
          make no choice, no analytics script loads and no analytics cookies are set.
        </p>
        <p>
          With consent, we send Google Analytics events such as page views, a “lead” event that
          includes the purpose you selected (never your name, email or ZIP code), and a “template
          opened” event that records whether you chose Google Sheets or Excel. Google acts as our
          analytics provider; see <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/6004245" rel="noopener">how Google safeguards Google Analytics data</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Bank search and the FDIC</h2>
        <p>
          When you search for banks by ZIP code, your browser sends the ZIP code you enter directly
          to the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation’s BankFind API, and the FDIC returns the
          matching institutions. We do not receive or store that ZIP code. The FDIC receives it,
          along with your IP address, as part of the request, and handles it under its own
          <a href="https://www.fdic.gov/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>. Nothing is sent to the FDIC
          until you run a search.
        </p>

        <h2>Hosting</h2>
        <p>
          The site is a static website served by GitHub Pages. GitHub may process technical
          request data, such as your IP address, when you load a page, as described in the
          <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub privacy statement</a>.
          Fonts and images are served from the site itself, not from third-party servers.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we share your data with</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell your personal data, and we do not share it with third parties for
          advertising or cross-context behavioral advertising. Your data is handled only by service providers that run the
          parts described above: Google (Sheets, Apps Script and mail for the form; Google
          Analytics, only with your consent) and GitHub (hosting). We may also disclose
          information if the law requires it or to protect our rights, users or the site.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we retain your data</h2>
        <p>
          We keep form submissions until you ask us to delete them or we no longer need them to
          run and improve the template. Analytics data is kept according to the retention setting
          of our Google Analytics 4 property. Your cookie choice stays in your browser until you
          clear it. Notification emails remain in the mailboxes of the team members who received
          them until they delete them.
        </p>

        <h2>How we protect your data</h2>
        <p>
          Form data travels over HTTPS to Google and is stored in Google’s infrastructure. Access
          to the Google Sheet is limited to the WorthSheet team. No method of transmission or
          storage is perfectly secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
        </p>

        <h2>What rights you have over your data</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us to tell you what personal data we hold about you, send you a copy, correct
          it, delete it, or stop contacting you. Email
          <a href={mailto}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> from the address you used on the form so we can find
          your record. We may need to confirm that the request comes from you, and we may keep what
          we are required to keep for legal or security reasons. We aim to respond within 45 days.
          You can withdraw analytics consent at any time with “Cookie settings” in the footer.
        </p>
        <h3>California residents (CCPA/CPRA)</h3>
        <p>
          California law gives you the right to know what personal information we collect, use and
          disclose; to request deletion or correction; to opt out of the sale or sharing of your
          personal information; to limit use of sensitive personal information; and to not be
          treated differently for using these rights. In the past 12 months we collected
          identifiers (name, email, ZIP code), internet activity (page, referrer and, with
          consent, analytics data) and the purpose you selected. We do not sell or share personal
          information as those terms are defined in California law, and we do not collect sensitive
          personal information. You may use an authorized agent to make a request on your behalf.
        </p>
        <h3>EEA, UK and similar laws</h3>
        <p>
          WorthSheet is aimed at people in the United States. If GDPR or a similar law applies to
          you, you also have the right to object to or restrict processing, to data portability and
          to complain to your local data protection authority. Our legal bases are your consent
          (analytics cookies, and the information you choose to submit in the form) and our
          legitimate interest in delivering and improving a free template. Because we use Google’s
          services, your data may be processed in the United States and other countries where
          Google operates.
        </p>

        <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
        <p>
          WorthSheet is not directed to children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect personal
          information from them. If you believe a child has submitted the form, email
          <a href={mailto}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> and we will delete the record.
        </p>

        <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>
          Our guides link to government and other third-party sites, such as the SBA, CFPB and
          FDIC. Those sites have their own privacy practices that we do not control.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If our practices change, we will update this page and the effective date above. Material
          changes will be reflected here before they take effect.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions or requests about your data: <a href={mailto}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Looking for
          the template? <a href={url('/download/')}>Get the free PFS template</a>.
        </p>
      </Prose>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>

<style>
  .policy-date {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .table-scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .table-scroll table {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 560px;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .table-scroll th,
  .table-scroll td {
    padding: 10px 12px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  .table-scroll thead th {
    background: var(--surface);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
